@mattcaswell It hasn't. It feels overkill, at least at this stage. What do we want to do? URI registration is specification required. If we want to register it, I'll need to write a spec and push it through the process.

Wondering what other OpenSSL store providers do.

> I'll need to write a spec and push it through the process.

My understanding is that it is sufficient to just create and register a draft spec. It doesn't necessarily need to be pushed all the way through the process (i.e. it can just remain as draft and then expire). So the spec doesn't even need to be that good!

@kaduk can probably advise on how to do it

